{title: Home on the Range}
{artist: Brewster M. Higley (words), Daniel E. Kelley (music)}
{key: G}
{time: 3/4}
{tempo: 100}
{meta: public_domain Words by Brewster M. Higley, written about 1872; music by Daniel E. Kelley.}
{meta: source John A. Lomax, Cowboy Songs and Other Frontier Ballads, 1910.}
{meta: arrangement Original chord arrangement for Fretlight}

{start_of_verse}
Oh, give me a [G]home where the [G]buffalo [C]roam,[C]
Where the [G]deer and the [G]antelope [D]play,[D]
Where [G]seldom is [G]heard a dis[C]couraging [C]word,
And the [G]skies are not [D]cloudy all [G]day.[G]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[D]Home, [D]home on the [G]range,[G]
Where the [G]deer and the [G]antelope [D]play,[D]
Where [G]seldom is [G]heard a dis[C]couraging [C]word,
And the [G]skies are not [D]cloudy all [G]day.[G]
{end_of_chorus}
